  "Question": "Twenty percent less than \\(60\\) is one-third more than what number?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(16\\)",
    "B": "\\(30\\)",
    "C": "\\(32\\)",
    "D": "\\(36\\)",
    "E": "\\(48\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "First find the amount described by “twenty percent less than \\(60\\)”:\n\\[\n60(1-0.20)=60(0.80)=48.\n\\]\nOne-third more than a number means the number plus one-third of itself. Thus \\(48\\) is \\(\\tfrac43\\) of the number we want. Dividing by this fraction gives\n\\[\n48\\div\\frac43=48\\cdot\\frac34=\\boxed{36}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice D.",
